# Financial Friday v0.6.0 Sprint – Advisor Architecture Blueprint

## Sprint Objective

Version **0.6.0** translates the completed Advisor Intelligence Specification (AIS) into an implementation-ready software architecture.

The objective of this sprint is to design the systems, data structures, interfaces, and workflows that will power the Financial Friday Advisor.

By the end of this sprint, every major component of the Advisor should have a clearly defined architecture, allowing future development to focus on implementation rather than design.

---

# Sprint Goals

## 1. Design the Advisor System Architecture

Create the high-level architecture that defines how every major Advisor component interacts.

### Deliverables

- Advisor System Architecture
- Component Interaction Diagram
- Architectural Principles

---

## 2. Define the Recommendation Pipeline

Translate the Advisor Decision Flow into an implementation-ready processing pipeline.

### Define

- Request processing
- Context building
- Recommendation generation
- Prioritization
- Confidence evaluation
- Transparency generation
- Response construction

### Deliverable

- Recommendation Pipeline Specification

---

## 3. Design the Domain Model

Define the core business objects that represent the Advisor's understanding of the user's financial life.

### Core Objects

- User
- Financial Profile
- Goal
- Recommendation
- Recommendation Outcome
- Financial Story
- Operating Mode
- Behavior Profile
- Evidence
- Opportunity
- Risk
- Priority Score
- Confidence
- Account
- Transaction
- Institution

### Deliverable

- Domain Model

---

## 4. Design Core Data Objects

Define the structure and relationships of the Advisor's primary data models.

### Define

- Object properties
- Relationships
- Ownership
- Lifecycles
- Serialization strategy
- Versioning considerations

### Deliverable

- Core Data Object Specifications

---

## 5. Define Advisor Engine Interfaces

Design the interfaces that separate each major responsibility within the Advisor.

### Components

- Recommendation Engine
- Priority Engine
- Confidence Engine
- Transparency Engine
- Memory Engine
- Behavior Engine
- Goal Engine
- Story Engine
- Operating Mode Engine

### Deliverable

- Engine Interface Specifications

---

## 6. Create Sequence Diagrams

Document how the Advisor processes common user scenarios.

### Example Flows

- Ask for financial advice
- Review finances
- Plan a home purchase
- Respond to a financial emergency
- Handle a windfall
- Update goals

### Deliverable

- Advisor Sequence Diagram Collection

---

## 7. Review and Refine the Existing Codebase

Evaluate the current implementation against the newly designed architecture.

### Tasks

- Identify architectural gaps
- Resolve unnecessary technical debt
- Improve project organization
- Remove obsolete code
- Confirm coding standards
- Prepare for implementation

### Deliverable

- Architecture Alignment Report

---

## 8. Create the Advisor Architecture Blueprint

Consolidate the architectural work into a single implementation guide.

### Contents

- System Architecture
- Recommendation Pipeline
- Domain Model
- Data Objects
- Engine Interfaces
- Sequence Diagrams
- Architectural Decisions
- Future Extension Points

### Deliverable

- Advisor Architecture Blueprint v1.0

---

# Success Criteria

The sprint is considered complete when:

- The Advisor System Architecture has been finalized.
- The Recommendation Pipeline has been documented.
- The Domain Model has been completed.
- Core Data Objects have been fully specified.
- Engine Interfaces have been defined.
- Sequence Diagrams cover the primary Advisor workflows.
- The existing codebase has been evaluated against the architecture.
- The Advisor Architecture Blueprint v1.0 has been completed.
- The project is ready to begin implementing the Advisor Kernel.

---

# Guiding Principles

During this sprint we will prioritize:

- Simplicity
- Separation of Concerns
- Scalability
- Extensibility
- Maintainability
- Transparency
- Testability
- Consistency

Every architectural decision should faithfully implement the principles established in the Constitution and the Advisor Intelligence Specification.

---

# Out of Scope

The following items are intentionally excluded from this sprint unless required by the architecture:

- Building the Advisor Engine
- AI prompt implementation
- Account integrations
- Budgeting features
- Investment tools
- UI redesign
- Production optimization
- Feature expansion

The focus of Version **0.6.0** is designing the system—not building it.

---

# Definition of Done

Version **0.6.0** is complete when the Advisor Intelligence Specification has been translated into a complete, implementation-ready software architecture.

The Advisor Architecture Blueprint should provide sufficient guidance for engineers to begin building the Advisor Kernel with minimal additional design work.

---

# Sprint Motto

> **"Design the architecture once. Build with confidence forever."**
